# Modern UI

Before coding a screen, generate it with Google Stitch MCP (skill `stitch-ui-design`).

Look: contemporary SaaS (clear hierarchy, generous whitespace, accessible contrast) — neighbourhood retail chemist console, not 2010 government portal, grey ERP, or dense data-entry grids as primary chrome. POS: large tap targets, keyboard-first.

```tsx
// BAD — spreadsheet-in-a-browser as the only layout
<table className="w-full text-xs text-gray-500">{/* 20 columns */}</table>

// GOOD — task-focused shell + identity
<header className="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
  <ShopIdentityBadge />
</header>
```

Do not invent a second design system. Use `shared-ui` + Tailwind. If Stitch is disconnected, stop the UI step — do not guess a legacy layout.
